For this task, I used Canva to design my digital literacy infographic because it is easy to use and provides many templates and icons. My design focuses on explaining the concept of digital literacy in a simple and visually attractive way for students. The infographic includes key topics such as what digital literacy means, useful digital tools for students, safe internet practices, professional online presence, and email etiquette.

I organized the content into separate sections using icons and short bullet points so that it is easy to understand at a glance. I used a clean color theme and simple layout to make the design look professional and engaging. The aim of my design is to help students become more aware of how to use digital tools effectively and safely in their academic and personal lives.

One interesting part of this task was selecting the right icons and layout to make the information visually appealing. However, I found it slightly difficult to keep the content brief while still covering all important points.
